WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.880
That is the Angel of the North - Antony Gormley's incredible sculpture

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.040
that stands as one of the icons of modern Britain.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.560
But angels aren't all like that - at least not in Christian philosophy.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.520
Pseudo-Dionysius the Areopagite - and I'm probably mispronouncing that,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.720
and no, that wasn't the name he went by then -

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.160
was a Christian writer in the fifth and sixth centuries

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:24.620
and he, along with Thomas Aquinas, settled on the modern Christian hierarchy of angels.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:29.600
And my word - if you wanted terrifying creatures you need look no further than angels

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:34.580
because yes, the ones in the lower orders, they look vaguely humanoid, as the term would be now:

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.200
but up at the top you have the cherubim.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.000
And they're not cherubs in the sense of angelic little children with serene expressions, no.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.540
They have four heads - a man, a lion, an eagle and an ox.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:51.260
And then you have the thrones - they don't look like that gorgeous thing

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.720
they look like a wheel within a wheel, covered in eyes.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.380
Seriously, if you wanted terrifying creatures from science fiction, it turns out that you can just go and look at some angels.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.080
This angel on the other hand is a lot prettier,

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.040
a lot nicer,

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:08.480
and frankly,

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.100
even though I'm not religious,

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:16.540
this is a greater testament to God's work than any wheel, within a wheel with eyes on it.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.860
From the Angel of the North, that is something you might not have known.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.880
One more thing before I go - thank you very much to everyone who replied to my call for help a couple of days ago

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.320
I got an order of magnitude more answers than I thought I would

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:34.300
You're all amazing, thank you so much and I'm sorry if I didn't get to your comment - I did the best I could.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:36.780
Oh and one more thing - if you want a bonus fact

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.500
There's as much of that angel below the ground as there is above.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.640
20 meters or so down to the bedrock.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.140
Otherwise? Well, the wind might just make it fly away.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.900
